  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U2.35", "U5.2", "U5.4", "U4.19", "U4.20", "R7.1"],
      "nets": ["DISP_SDA", "Net-(U5-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The netlist inserts U5, a 74LVC1G34 single buffer gate, between the MCU display-SDA pin and the OLED SDA pins. U2 pin 35 (PB14) is connected only to U5 pin 2 on net Net-(U5-Pad2), while U5 pin 4 drives net DISP_SDA together with U4 pins 19/20 and R7. The MCU pin is not directly on DISP_SDA.",
      "expected": "The specification states that DISP_SDA is directly connected to U2 pin 35 (PB14), R7 to VCC, and U4 pins 19/20 (D1/D2). An I2C SDA line should be a shared bidirectional/open-drain bus, not isolated by a unidirectional buffer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "DISP_SDA: U2 pin 35 (`PB14`) — R7 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U4 pins 19/20 (`D1`/`D2`)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U5\") (value \"74LVC1G34\") ... (description \"Single Buffer Gate, Low-Voltage CMOS\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"DISP_SDA\") ... (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"4\") (pintype \"output\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"24\") (name \"Net-(U5-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"35\") (pinfunction \"PB14\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The OLED SDA bus is separated from the MCU by a one-way buffer. The MCU cannot read or be driven by the display's SDA/ACK, the MCU-side line lacks the specified pull-up connection, and the intended bidirectional I2C display interface is broken or behaves differently from the reference design.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: U5, an unlisted 74LVC1G34 buffer, is inserted between the MCU's DISP_SDA pin and the OLED SDA bus, contradicting the specified direct bidirectional I2C connection."
}

